menu "AM Transmitter"

    config AMTX_WIFI_SSID
        string "Fallback Wi-Fi SSID"
        default ""
        help
            Used only when NVS holds no saved network. Leave empty and use the
            AMTX-Setup portal instead. Whatever you put here ends up in
            sdkconfig, which is gitignored for exactly that reason.

    config AMTX_WIFI_PASS
        string "Fallback Wi-Fi password"
        default ""

    config AMTX_STATION_A_NAME
        string "Transmitter A's starting station: name"
        default "Radio Swiss Jazz"

    config AMTX_STATION_A_URL
        string "Transmitter A's starting station: URL"
        default "http://stream.srg-ssr.ch/m/rsj/mp3_128"
        help
            Seeded into the station list on a factory-fresh device and made
            transmitter A's power-on station. Plain HTTP MP3: the stream
            client attaches no certificate bundle. Leave empty to seed
            nothing for A. See docs/design/07_console_and_access.md section 5.

    config AMTX_STATION_B_NAME
        string "Transmitter B's starting station: name"
        default "BBC World Service"

    config AMTX_STATION_B_URL
        string "Transmitter B's starting station: URL"
        default "http://stream.live.vc.bbcmedia.co.uk/bbc_world_service"
        help
            As for transmitter A, seeded second and made transmitter B's
            power-on station.

    config AMTX_RF_GPIO
        int "RF carrier output GPIO"
        default 4
        range 0 48
        help
            Drives the carrier through the output low-pass network. Avoid the
            strapping pins (0, 3, 45, 46) and the USB pins (19, 20).

    config AMTX_RF_GPIO_B
        int "Second RF carrier output GPIO"
        default 5
        range 0 48
        help
            Drives the second carrier through its own output low-pass network.
            The two carriers are independent transmitters and each needs its
            own filter: sharing one lets them intermodulate. Same pins to
            avoid as the first (strapping 0, 3, 45, 46; USB 19, 20).

    config AMTX_FACTORY_BUTTON_GPIO
        int "Factory reset button GPIO"
        default 0
        range 0 48
        help
            The BOOT button on an ESP32-S3-Zero, marked B on the silkscreen.
            Held for the time below while the board is running, it erases
            everything saved and restarts. Pressed is LOW.

            This is a strapping pin, and holding it through a RESET is what
            puts the chip into the ROM's download mode instead. That is the
            ROM's behaviour, not this firmware's, and it is why the gesture
            here is a long press while running. See design 07 section 7.

    config AMTX_FACTORY_HOLD_MS
        int "Factory reset hold time (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 1000 30000
        help
            Longer than an accidental press, shorter than anyone's patience.
            The console counts down once a second while the button is held.

    config AMTX_LPF_CUTOFF_HZ
        int "Audio low-pass cutoff (Hz)"
        default 4500
        range 1000 9000
        help
            Anything above this becomes adjacent-channel splatter. 4500 keeps
            the transmission inside a 9 kHz channel.

endmenu
